the coalesced layouts are ranked where the rate and the capacity both resolve: true
not without the workgroup capacity: true
not without the transaction rate: true
not without the launch fill's multiprocessor count, which the occupancy factor reads: true
not without the device residency: true
not without a lane width: true
the coalesced layouts are ranked through the staged-copy rate, without a capacity: true
not without the staged-copy rate (and no capacity): true
not through the copy rate without the launch fill it prices with: true
not through the copy rate without the transaction rate: true
the coalesced layouts are ranked on discrete RDNA wave32 HIP (tuf): true
not on discrete RDNA wave32 HIP without the transaction rate: true
the uncoalesced walk returns an uncoalesced leaf: true
with the coalesced menu, the pick ranks no higher than the uncoalesced walk's: true
on tuf_like at outproj b8, the coalesced walk picks 64x64x32/4x4 bgrid coal-k: true
on tuf_like at outproj b8, the uncoalesced walk picks 32x32x8/4x4 bgrid: true
dropping staged_idle_rate on tuf_like flips the uncoalesced b8 pick to 64x64x8/4x4 bgrid: true
dropping workgroup capacity on tuf_like flips the coalesced b8 pick to 64x64x128/4x4 bgrid coal-k: true
under the staged-copy rate, a coal-k leaf strictly beats the uncoalesced walk's pick at b256: true
without it, both walks return a pick, the uncoalesced one uncoalesced, and the coalesced menu's ranks no lower: true
on tuf_like at outproj b256, the coalesced walk picks 64x64x32/4x4 bgrid coal-k: true
on tuf_like at outproj b256, the uncoalesced walk picks 32x32x8/4x4 bgrid: true
dropping staged_idle_rate on tuf_like flips the uncoalesced b256 pick to 64x64x8/4x4 bgrid: true
dropping workgroup capacity on tuf_like flips the coalesced b256 pick to 64x64x128/4x4 bgrid coal-k: true
